<main>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how information is
    handled in ODD ROOTS, an Android mobile game
    developed by an independent developer.
  </p>
  <p>
    We respect your privacy and aim to be transparent
    about data processing associated with the game.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Offline Gameplay</h2>
  <p>
    ODD ROOTS is designed to support offline gameplay.
    Game progress, settings and unlockable content
    are intended to be stored locally on your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Advertising features, when enabled, may require
    an internet connection.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising and Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    The game is planned to use Google AdMob,
    provided by Google, to display advertisements.
    These may include optional rewarded advertisements
    that players choose to watch in exchange for
    in-game benefits.
  </p>
  <p>
    When Google Mobile Ads SDK is enabled, it may
    automatically collect and share information
    such as:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>IP address and approximate location inferred from it;</li>
    <li>Advertising identifiers and other device identifiers;</li>
    <li>App interactions and advertising interactions;</li>
    <li>Diagnostic and performance information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This information may be processed for advertising,
    measurement, analytics, fraud prevention and
    service improvement, subject to the applicable
    Google policies and user privacy choices.
  </p>
  <p>
    Learn more:
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
      Google Privacy Policy
    </a>
    and
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">
      How Google uses information from apps
      that use its services
    </a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Accounts and Personal Information</h2>
  <p>
    ODD ROOTS is designed not to require users to
    create an account or provide their name, email
    address or phone number to play.
  </p>
  <p>
    Information may nevertheless be processed by
    third-party advertising services as described
    above.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>
    Local gameplay information is used to maintain
    progress, settings and unlocked content.
  </p>
  <p>
    Advertising-related information may be used
    by Google and its advertising partners to
    deliver advertisements, measure performance,
    detect invalid activity and maintain services.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    The game is not designed to sell player account
    information or gameplay saves.
  </p>
  <p>
    When advertising is enabled, Google and
    applicable advertising partners may receive
    data through the advertising SDK.
    Their processing is governed by their
    applicable privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to limit data processing to what is
    necessary for game functionality and enabled
    third-party services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google Mobile Ads SDK uses encryption in transit
    for data it transmits. No electronic storage
    or transmission method can be guaranteed
    completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Locally stored game progress and settings may
    remain on the device until the relevant game
    data is cleared or the app is uninstalled.
    Device backups may be subject to Android
    backup settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not plan to maintain player accounts
    or a developer-operated database of personal
    player information.
  </p>
  <p>
    Information processed by Google or its
    advertising partners is retained according
    to their respective policies.
    For questions about information handled
    directly by the developer, please contact
    the email address below.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your Privacy Choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may manage advertising-related preferences
    using available Android and Google privacy
    controls. Where required, the game will
    provide applicable consent choices before
    requesting advertising services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Rewarded advertisements are intended to be
    optional. Players may decline them.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The game's intended audience and age rating
    will be established before publication.
    Any advertising and data processing must
    comply with the requirements applicable
    to the selected audience.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy when game
    features, third-party services or legal
    requirements change.
  </p>
  <p>
    The latest version will be published on
    this page with an updated revision date.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests,
    contact the ODD ROOTS developer:
  </p>
